      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Optimizing for \"equality of outcome\" can actually be ethically problematic rather than the most sound approach, as it often sacrifices fairness for equality and may lead to unintended systemic distortions.\n\nIsolating your model from the rest of the system is an anti-pattern that reduces the ability of the model to be effective and results in a solution that is unnecessarily complicated to maintain.\n\nI recommend setting clear ethical constraints on your algorithm that you don't want to violate, then ensuring your model adheres to those guardrails.\n\nYou could also look at how fair modeling and algorithmic accountability guidelines align with your broader ESG mission to make a decision that is both responsible and practical.",
